1
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Consider the Possibilities

2
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Bob & Carol & Ted & Alice is a comedy, drama film directed by Paul Mazursky.

3
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:36,000
After returning to Los Angeles from a group therapy session, documentary filmmaker Bob Sanders and his wife, Carol, find themselves
becoming vigilante couples counselors, offering unsolicited advice to their best friends, Ted and Alice Henderson.

4
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Not wanting to be rude, the Hendersons play along, but some latent sexual tension among the four soon
comes bubbling to the surface, and long-buried desires don't stay buried for long.

5
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Carol Sanders, played by Natalie Wood.

6
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Bob Sanders, played by Robert Culp.

7
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:56,000
Ted Henderson, played by Elliott Gould.

8
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Alice Henderson, played by Dyan Cannon.

9
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Horst, played by Horst Ebersberg.

10
00:58:20,000 --> 00:58:26,000
Emilio, played by Lee Bergere.

11
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
Bob & Carol & Ted & Alice is a 1969 American comedy-drama film directed by Paul Mazursky, written by Mazursky and Larry
Tucker, who also produced the film, and starring Natalie Wood, Robert Culp, Elliott Gould, and Dyan Cannon.

12
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The original music score was composed by Quincy Jones.

13
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
The cinematography for the film was by Charles Lang.

14
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:46,000
The film received four Academy Award nominations,
including ones for Gould and Cannon.

15
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
Patricia Welles wrote the paperback novelization
from Mazursky and Tucker's screenplay.

16
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
The film explores themes of friends, therapy, polyamory, foursome.

17
01:39:10,000 --> 01:39:16,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
